{"blocks":[["Arturia/MCC/UG/03%20Working%20with%20Templates/03%20Project%20and%20Template%20Browser/","source-block-308","The browser holds archived Templates on the computer in Factory and User groups. A Template usually mirrors the device memory layout, though some devices hold multiple Templates.",["3.3. Project / Template Browser"]],["Arturia/MCC/UG/03%20Working%20with%20Templates/03%20Project%20and%20Template%20Browser/","source-block-490","Templates do not include Device Settings.",["3.3. Project / Template Browser"]],["Arturia/MCC/UG/03%20Working%20with%20Templates/03%20Project%20and%20Template%20Browser/01%20Device%20Templates/","source-block-238","3.3.1. Device Templates",[]],["Arturia/MCC/UG/03%20Working%20with%20Templates/03%20Project%20and%20Template%20Browser/01%20Device%20Templates/","source-block-266","A Template may contain several data layers. Expand or collapse them with the browser’s plus and minus controls.",["3.3.1. Device Templates"]],["Arturia/MCC/UG/03%20Working%20with%20Templates/03%20Project%20and%20Template%20Browser/02%20Build%20Library/","source-block-343","3.3.2. Building a library",[]]],"format_version":5}